myelin 1
id      python-safe-http
about   Python HTTP calls with timeouts, status checks, and TLS left on
fires   python requests | http client | python api call
status  Demo ledger. Regex-level checks only; "unless" is unit-wide, so one timeout= in a file exempts every call in it.

= python.min   3.9

! H1 /requests\.(get|post|put|patch|delete|head)\(/ unless /timeout\s*=/   Every requests call sets timeout=. -> $client
! H2 /verify\s*=\s*False/              Never disable TLS verification.
! H3 /^\s*except\s*:/m                 No bare except. Catch a named exception. -> $client
+ H4 /raise_for_status\(\)/            Check the response status. -> $client

~ P1 Reuse a requests.Session for several calls to one host.

$ client
import requests


def fetch_json(url: str, timeout: float = 10.0) -> dict:
    resp = requests.get(url, timeout=timeout)
    resp.raise_for_status()
    return resp.json()


def try_fetch(url: str):
    try:
        return fetch_json(url)
    except requests.RequestException:
        return None
